    "result_text": "The build succeeds and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `riskFlag` field on owners so it returns `true` when **any** of the three conditions hold, and `false` otherwise.\n\n**Interpretation of the three conditions** (grounded in the existing code vocabulary):\n1. **Possible duplicate** \u2192 the stored `possibleDuplicate` flag (existing soft-duplicate detection).\n2. **Disposable-adjacent email domain** \u2192 a domain that isn't on the exact disposable blocklist (those are already rejected at create time), but is a variant of a known disposable provider \u2014 a subdomain of a blocklisted domain, or one sharing a blocklisted provider's second-level label under a different TLD (e.g. `mailinator.net`, `sub.tempmail.com`). This makes the condition meaningful for stored owners, which a literal \"on the blocklist\" reading could never be.\n3. **City over its soft capacity** \u2192 the existing soft-capacity threshold (40, the same limit that raises `capacityWarning`).\n\n**Changes:**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added the `riskFlag` readOnly boolean to the `Owner` schema (the `OwnerDto` is generated from this at build).\n- `OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 ignored `riskFlag` in the mapping (like the other derived flags `capacityWarning`/`bulkSignupWarning`).\n- `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` \u2014 added `isDisposableAdjacent(...)` / `secondLevelLabel(...)` helpers (deriving disposable provider labels from the existing blocklist so they stay in sync) and a `computeRiskFlag(...)` helper, then set `riskFlag` on the DTO at every response-building site (create, idempotent-return, get, update, list) \u2014 mirroring exactly how `capacityWarning` is populated.\n\n`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`. The provided `coreRiskFlagFalseNormally` test (a normal owner with no email, unique identity, and an empty city) correctly yields `riskFlag: false`.",
